# SimpleHandler

`SimpleHandler` is the default `handlerComponent` of the stencils: the small square drawn at each corner and edge of the stencil, which the user drags to resize it. [`BoundingBox`](/docs/components/BoundingBox) renders one per enabled handler and passes it the props below. The handler draws itself inside an invisible, larger hit area that shows the right resize cursor.

```
BoundingBox
└─ div.advanced-cropper-bounding-box__handler-wrapper--{direction}
   └─ SimpleHandler
      └─ HandlerWrapper (hit area) → DraggableElement
         └─ div.advanced-cropper-simple-handler
```

## Usage

The quickest way to restyle the handlers is with classes, through the stencil's `handlerClassNames` and `handlerWrapperClassNames`, or with a [theme](/docs/guides/themes). See [Customize Appearance](/docs/guides/customize-appearance#handler).

To draw something entirely different, pass your own component as `handlerComponent` in `stencilProps`. It receives the props below and must forward drags to `onMove` and `onMoveEnd`. The easiest way is to wrap your markup in `HandlerWrapper`, the hit area `SimpleHandler` uses, which this package exports (react-advanced-cropper keeps it internal):

```svelte
<!-- DotHandler.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
	import { HandlerWrapper, type HandlerComponentProps } from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';

	let {
		horizontalPosition,
		verticalPosition,
		wrapperClassName,
		disabled,
		onMove,
		onMoveEnd
	}: HandlerComponentProps = $props();
</script>

<HandlerWrapper
	class={wrapperClassName}
	{horizontalPosition}
	{verticalPosition}
	{disabled}
	onDrag={onMove}
	onDragEnd={onMoveEnd}
>
	<div class="dot-handler"></div>
</HandlerWrapper>

<style>
	.dot-handler {
		width: 12px;
		height: 12px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: white;
	}
</style>
```

```svelte
<Cropper {src} stencilProps={{ handlerComponent: DotHandler }} />
```

## Props

These are the props `BoundingBox` passes to every handler component (the exported `HandlerComponentProps` type).

| Prop                 | Type                                                                   | Description                                                                                                       |
| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `horizontalPosition` | `'east'` \| `'west'` \| `null`                                          | The horizontal side of the handler, or `null` for the north and south handlers.                                   |
| `verticalPosition`   | `'north'` \| `'south'` \| `null`                                        | The vertical side of the handler, or `null` for the east and west handlers.                                       |
| `disabled`           | `boolean`                                                              | `true` when the stencil can't be resized.                                                                         |
| `onMove`             | <code>(shift: MoveDirections, event: MouseEvent &#124; TouchEvent) =&gt; void</code> | Call it with each drag step.                                                                                      |
| `onMoveEnd`          | `() => void`                                                           | Call it when the drag ends.                                                                                       |
| `defaultClassName`   | `ClassValue`                                                           | Classes for the handler element, from `handlerClassNames.default` and the handler's own direction key.            |
| `hoverClassName`     | `ClassValue`                                                           | Classes to add while hovered, from `handlerClassNames.hover`.                                                     |
| `wrapperClassName`   | `ClassValue`                                                           | Classes for the hit area: the `BoundingBox` handler classes plus `handlerWrapperClassNames`.                     |
| `wrapperStyle`       | `string`                                                               | Inline style for the hit area. `BoundingBox` doesn't pass it; it is there for using `SimpleHandler` on its own.    |

## CSS classes

`{v}` stands for `north` or `south`, and `{h}` for `east` or `west`.

| Element  | Classes                                                                                                                                                                  |
| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Hit area | `advanced-cropper-handler-wrapper`, `advanced-cropper-handler-wrapper--{h}-{v}` (or `--{h}`, `--{v}`), `advanced-cropper-handler-wrapper--disabled`                      |
| Hit area | `advanced-cropper-simple-handler-wrapper`, `--{v}`, `--{h}`, `--{h}-{v}`, and `--hover` while hovered                                                                    |
| Handler  | `advanced-cropper-simple-handler`, `--{v}`, `--{h}`, `--{h}-{v}`, and `--hover` while hovered                                                                            |

The modifiers are appended to the class before them, as in `advanced-cropper-simple-handler--east-north`. The hit area is a 30×30 pixel box centered on its point, with a resize cursor for its direction. The handler's look (size, color, hover effect) comes from the theme.
